  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** GrowGeneration is in the early stages of a commercial-led recovery, with its B2B sales channel now the primary growth engine and driving consecutive quarters of year-over-year expansion. Rising penetration of proprietary brands is strengthening the quality of cultivation and gardening revenue. Demand remains seasonal, yet core operations are stabilizing after a difficult industry downturn. The company is benefiting from a focused controlled-environment agriculture niche, though macro and regulatory uncertainty in the cannabis-adjacent market continues to shape the cautious recovery.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is executing a deliberate turnaround, emphasizing cost discipline, asset-light efficiency, and a shift toward higher-margin proprietary products. The team reaffirmed full-year guidance for near-breakeven profitability, signaling confidence in its trajectory. Recent governance moves—including shareholder approval of an equity plan amendment—support retention and alignment. Management’s messaging reflects steady progress in transforming a once-distressed operator into a leaner, commercially oriented supplier, which is gradually rebuilding credibility.",
